            <H2><FONT color=3D#000000><A name=3Dexample_one></A>Example =
1:=20
            Interrupting a Swing Worker Thread </FONT></H2>
            <P></P>
            <P><FONT color=3D#000000>This section features an example =
called <A=20
            =
href=3D"http://java.sun.com/products/jfc/tsc/articles/threads/src/Example=
1.java"><FONT=20
            face=3D"Courier =
New,Courier"><TT>Example1.java</TT></FONT></A>. The=20
            worker thread in this example contains a loop that executes =
100=20
            times, sleeping for half a second each time.</FONT></P>
            <UL>
              <P><FONT face=3D"Courier New,Courier"=20
              color=3D#000000><TT><BR>//progressBar maximum is NUMLOOPS=20
              (100)<BR>for(int i =3D 0; i &lt; NUMLOOPS; i++) =
{<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;=20
              updateStatus(i);<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp; ...<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;=20
              Thread.sleep(500);<BR>}</TT></FONT></P></UL>
            <P><FONT color=3D#000000>To show you how to use the <FONT=20
            face=3D"Courier New,Courier"><TT>interrupt()</TT></FONT> =
method, we've=20
            created an application that lets you start a SwingWorker and =
then=20
            either wait for it to complete or interrupt it. In this=20
            application's subclass of SwingWorker, the only thing the =
